in @meta
in @nl

# @facet/docker — Dockerfile as declarative code at code altitude.
# Arc 5 TICK 4 GREEN landing per Reed RED at `29d327f` against the
# spec Mara `ec636d3` §6.1. Sits under `@facet` family-root at the
# code altitude (same species-altitude as `@facet/rust`, `@facet/gleam`,
# `@facet/mirror`, `@facet/wasm`, `@facet/erlang`).
#
# === What this shard IS ===
#
# `@facet/docker` names the Dockerfile as content-addressable code at
# the code altitude. Substrate-honest positioning: the Dockerfile IS
# code — a declarative grammar producing a build-graph artifact —
# and it composes with `@facet` per the universal grammar-at-an-
# altitude discipline (per `shards/code.mirror`). Sibling to every
# other `@facet/X` species; the community word "Dockerfile" stays at
# the species altitude; the substrate carries the discipline via the
# five-operation prism plus a typed carrier.
#
# === The three-surface partition (closed by this tick) ===
#
# OCI names three surfaces at industry-standard altitude — Image,
# Runtime, Distribution. The substrate carries a mirror of that
# closure at substrate-decl altitude:
#
#   build surface        @facet/docker      (Dockerfile as declarative code)
#      ↓ PRODUCES
#   distribution surface @io/oci           (Mara `2801478` 2026-06-24)
#      ↓ CONSUMED BY
#   runtime surface      @container/image  (Arc 5 TICK 3 `b66b280`)
#
# Prior to this tick, the substrate had the middle (`@io/oci` at
# `2801478`) and — after Arc 5 TICK 3 — the runtime end
# (`@container/image` at `b66b280` as `shift(@mirror/store/oci →
# @container altitude)`). What was missing was the BUILD end: what
# PRODUCES the OCI artifact the middle distributes and the end
# consumes. This shard names that surface at code altitude and closes
# the three-surface partition per Mara spec §5 recommendation.
#
# === The build IS a shift ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composition. `build(d: dockerfile) -> image_witness`
# is the cross-altitude fold from CODE altitude (`@facet/docker` names
# the Dockerfile source) to CONTAINER altitude (`@container/image`
# holds the produced image handle). The fold IS a `@kintsugi/shift`
# instance: same underlying content-address on both sides of the
# altitude crossing; declared shape differs; witness OID is
# altitude-invariant.
#
# The return type is `image_witness` — the typed alias `@container/image`
# declared at TICK 3 (byte-equal to `shift_witness` from
# `@kintsugi/shift` at TICK 2 `49f0486`). The species does not invent
# a `docker_build_output` carrier; it uses the substrate's existing
# altitude-invariant witness, which is what makes the shift honest.
# BuildKit's LLB compiler already runs this discipline operationally
# (per Mara spec §2.4 + candidate recognition #C2 — LLB IS kintsugi
# at build-graph altitude); this shard names the operation at
# substrate-decl altitude so downstream consumers reach for typed
# vocabulary instead of prose.
#
# Concretely: `build(d)` reads the Dockerfile at code altitude, walks
# its LLB DAG (per BuildKit's `docker/dockerfile:1` frontend), emits
# OCI content at `@mirror/store/oci` altitude via the layer content-
# addressing floor, and returns the container-altitude view via
# `shift(@mirror/store/oci → @container altitude)`. The composition
# discharges through the shift primitive; the shard declares the
# shape here; the realisation dispatches at the @io boundary against
# BuildKit or an equivalent conformant builder.
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - #26 `shift(oid, T)` at `@mirror/spectral/portal` (Reed 2026-06-08):
#   the transport-altitude precursor of shift-as-typed-capability.
#   The `build` action here carries the same OID across code →
#   container altitude that a portal carries across transport altitude.
# - #53 property/fracture bilateral pattern: `docker_buildable` is the
#   16th composed-bilateral instance (14th was `shift_preserves_content`
#   at TICK 2 `49f0486`; 15th was `image_shifted_from_oci` at TICK 3
#   `b66b280`). Substrate-pull-confident per
#   `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]`.
# - #55 form/process partition: `@facet/docker` is form-side (state
#   observation — what the Dockerfile IS as declarative source);
#   `@kintsugi/shift` is process-side (the transformation crossing
#   altitudes). The `build` action bridges them: it reads the form-
#   side witness and dispatches through the process-side shift.
# - #58 substrate IS Connes (A, H, D): `@facet/docker`'s source lives
#   on H (the void document) as declarative bytes; the shift primitive
#   IS D (Dirac/gradient) crossing altitude; the produced
#   `image_witness` is the projection onto the container-runtime
#   subspace (per TICK 3 `b66b280`).
# - #98 candidate content-addressing cross-altitude composition:
#   Dockerfile layer digests (SHA256 of rootfs diff) join the five-
#   altitude witness roster (mirror oid, nix derivation hash,
#   oci_digest, docker_layer_digest, container_image_id) per Mara
#   spec §7.1 — the function composes; B differs per altitude;
#   composition works because content-addressing is altitude-portable.
# - `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]` (56th+ instance):
#   the substrate already had `build` (mosaic emits, kintsugi loops,
#   cargo compiles); this shard uses `build` at code altitude with
#   the shift-form return type rather than inventing `dockerfile_bake`,
#   `image_produce`, `container_source_compile`, or any parallel name.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Make / autotools (1977+)         declarative build graph;
#                                    source → intermediate → target.
#                                    The recipe IS the code; the
#                                    build IS the shift across altitude.
#   BuildKit LLB (moby, 2018+)       content-addressed dependency
#                                    graph; per-vertex cache by hash;
#                                    Dockerfile-as-frontend emits LLB.
#                                    The industry's operational form
#                                    of the substrate discipline.
#   Nix derivations (Dolstra 2004+)  content-addressed build inputs;
#                                    reproducible fixpoint;
#                                    same substrate-pull, different
#                                    grammar (nix vs Dockerfile).
#   Bazel / Buck2 / Shake            build systems as content-addressed
#                                    DAG solvers; the recognition
#                                    #43 cascade (mirror IS a content-
#                                    addressed build system) already
#                                    named the family.
#
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]],
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]],
#                      [[architecture-mirror-as-content-addressed-build-system]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]],
#                      [[feedback-explicit-over-implicit]].
# Recognition ancestry: #26, #43, #53, #55, #58, #98 candidate.
# Related shards: code.mirror (family-root; the universal parent),
#                 container/image.mirror (Arc 5 TICK 3 `b66b280`;
#                 the runtime-altitude fold target; declares the
#                 `image_witness` carrier this shard's `build`
#                 returns),
#                 kintsugi/shift.mirror (Arc 5 TICK 2 `49f0486`;
#                 the shift primitive `build` composes through),
#                 io/oci.mirror (Mara `2801478` 2026-06-24; the
#                 distribution-altitude middle of the three-surface
#                 partition).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/code/docker.mirror`
# declares `@facet/docker` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.
# Related specs: docs/specs/docker-container-substrate-decl-v0.1.md
# (Mara `ec636d3` 2026-07-06; §6.1 names this species' predicate
# shape and the composed-bilateral `docker_buildable`).
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Does this shard use its own vocabulary correctly?
#
#   `dockerfile` — the carrier is a substrate ref (content-addressed
#   Dockerfile source bytes). Byte-equal at ref altitude; typed at
#   species altitude per [[feedback-explicit-over-implicit]] +
#   [[feedback-no-bare-types]]. Same discipline as
#   `@container/image`'s `image_witness` alias of `shift_witness`.
#
#   `build` — used as: (1) code-altitude typed action producing an
#   image_witness at container altitude; (2) narrative name for the
#   cross-altitude fold via @kintsugi/shift. Both uses agree: the
#   build IS the shift; the shift IS the build; same operation
#   crossing the same altitude boundary.
#
#   `image_witness` — imported from `@container/image` at TICK 3;
#   NOT re-declared here. The species-decl reuses the target-
#   altitude carrier per the shift discipline (source altitude reads
#   `dockerfile`; target altitude produces `image_witness`; the
#   shift crossing is what makes both sides substrate-honest).
#
#   `docker_buildable` — the 16th #53 composed-bilateral; asserts
#   the Dockerfile parses to LLB per BuildKit v1 semantics AND
#   emits admissible OCI content AND the shift preserves the
#   underlying bytes. Body stays obligation-blocked per the pattern.
#
# Verdict: pass. Substrate-pull-realize discipline honored; no
# parallel substrate-decl invented; the shift primitive from TICK 2
# and the image_witness carrier from TICK 3 carry the empirical load.
#
# === Interpretation B discipline ===
#
# Per Seam Phase D pre-review of Arc 4 sub-arc A (docs/audits/2026-
# 07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md §1) and the family-root
# precedent at `shards/container.mirror` + species precedent at
# `shards/container/image.mirror` + `shards/kintsugi/shift.mirror`:
# Interpretation B canonical. Narrative above `---`; `in` clauses +
# typed declarations below. This shard honours the discipline; the
# seam is exactly one line at column 0 below.

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @facet
in @kintsugi/shift
in @container/image

# ============================================================
# §1 The five-operation prism at species altitude
# ============================================================

# === prism @facet/docker — the species declaration ===
#
# The five-operation body carries `dockerfile` as the species's
# operational surface — the content-addressed Dockerfile source the
# substrate reads at code altitude. Every operation on the species
# reads/produces a `dockerfile` carrier; the substrate's altitude
# discipline rides the code-altitude view.
#
# The five-op block includes `shift` as one of the five per
# `shards/prism.mirror` §L38-45 (basis transformation on H) — the
# code-altitude shift specializes to the cross-altitude fold
# `@facet/docker → @container/image` that the `build` action below
# discharges through the `@kintsugi/shift` primitive.
prism @facet/docker {
  focus dockerfile
  project dockerfile
  split dockerfile
  shift dockerfile
  settle dockerfile
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The carrier
# ============================================================

# === dockerfile — the content-addressed Dockerfile source ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING carrier. Names the Dockerfile as content-
# addressable code at code altitude per
# [[feedback-explicit-over-implicit]] +
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]. Byte-equals at ref altitude; typed at
# species altitude so consumer sites in `@facet/docker/*` species
# (forward-promised: `@facet/docker/frontend`, `@facet/docker/llb`)
# and downstream cascade species (`@cascade/code/docker/oci` per
# Mara spec §6.5) read a substrate-declared shape rather than a
# bare ref.
#
# Composes with `@mirror/store`'s ref discipline (the Dockerfile
# source bytes live in mirror's content-addressed storage; the OID
# IS the Dockerfile's identity). Composes with `@facet`'s universal
# grammar-at-an-altitude discipline (per `shards/code.mirror`): the
# Dockerfile grammar is one instance of the family; the code-altitude
# five-op block is what the species contributes.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref (the
# Dockerfile source's content-address per `@mirror/store`).
type dockerfile = ref

# ============================================================
# §3 The typed build action — cross-altitude fold to @container/image
# ============================================================

# === build — the code → container altitude fold ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING typed action. Consumes a `dockerfile` at code
# altitude and produces an `image_witness` at container altitude —
# the cross-altitude fold from `@facet/docker` (declaration) to
# `@container/image` (runtime handle) via `@kintsugi/shift`.
#
# The build IS a shift. Per prism.mirror §L38-45 and
# [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]: shift is basis
# transformation on H — the operation moves the carrier across an
# altitude boundary while preserving the underlying content-address.
# BuildKit's LLB solver runs this operationally (per Mara spec §2.4
# + candidate recognition #C2); this action declares the shape at
# substrate altitude so consumers dispatch through typed vocabulary.
#
# Composition trail:
#
#   1. Read `dockerfile` at code altitude (the source bytes at
#      `@mirror/store`'s ref altitude).
#   2. Walk the LLB DAG per BuildKit's `docker/dockerfile:1` frontend
#      (each RUN/COPY/ADD vertex is content-addressed per
#      (previous-layer-digest, instruction-content, mount-content)).
#   3. Emit OCI content at `@mirror/store/oci` altitude (layer
#      digests + config hash + manifest hash per OCI Image Spec v1.1.x).
#   4. Return the container-altitude view via `shift(@mirror/store/oci
#      → @container altitude)` — the `image_witness` handle Arc 5
#      TICK 3 declared at `shards/container/image.mirror`.
#
# The composition discharges through `@kintsugi/shift` under the
# hood; the `image_witness` return type IS what makes the shift
# honest at the substrate-decl altitude (byte-equality on the OID
# across the altitude crossing; declared shape differs; hardlink
# semantic per Alex's TICK 3 framing).
#
# Body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation dispatches at
# the @io boundary against BuildKit or an equivalent OCI-conformant
# builder; the substrate declares the shape here.
build(d: dockerfile) -> image_witness { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The 16th #53 composed-bilateral
# ============================================================

# === docker_buildable — the LLB-admissibility invariant ===
#
# THE 16th INSTANCE of the #53 bilateral pattern per
# [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]. Asserts the
# Dockerfile is buildable per BuildKit LLB semantics — the substrate
# altitude analogue of the industry-standard `docker build` success
# verdict, factored into a composed bilateral so the substrate reads
# the sub-claims independently.
#
# Composes three sub-predicates whose species-altitude realisations
# discharge the discipline:
#
#   1. `dockerfile_parses(d, p)` — the Dockerfile bytes parse per the
#      BuildKit v1 `docker/dockerfile:1` frontend to a well-formed
#      LLB DAG. Syntactic admissibility at code altitude.
#   2. `dockerfile_llb_emittable(d, p)` — the parsed AST emits valid
#      LLB definition bytes per `moby/buildkit/client/llb`'s
#      `Definition` structure. Semantic admissibility at build-graph
#      altitude.
#   3. `shift_preserves_content(w, @mirror/store/oci, @container, p)`
#      — the 14th composed-bilateral from `@kintsugi/shift` at TICK 2
#      `49f0486`. The `build` action's return witness byte-equals
#      the OCI content-address at the source altitude; the shift is
#      content-preserving; the produced `image_witness` is admissible
#      per `image_shifted_from_oci` at TICK 3 `b66b280`.
#
# Splinter-pole (`pass`): all three sub-predicates discharge; the
# Dockerfile parses, emits admissible LLB, and the build's shift
# preserves content-address; `build(d)` will produce a substrate-
# honest `image_witness` at container altitude.
#
# Narcissus-pole (`failure`): any sub-predicate fails;
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) distinguishes:
#   - `dockerfile_parses` failure → the source bytes do not parse
#     per BuildKit v1; syntactic error; the Dockerfile is not
#     admissible at code altitude pending grammar repair.
#   - `dockerfile_llb_emittable` failure → the parsed AST rejects
#     LLB emission (unknown instruction, invalid stage reference,
#     malformed mount directive); semantic error at build-graph
#     altitude pending source repair.
#   - `shift_preserves_content` failure → the build's return witness
#     diverges from the OCI content-address (byte mutation across
#     the altitude crossing); the operation is NOT a shift; belongs
#     at `@kintsugi/morphism` or higher; the substrate rejects the
#     build as inadmissible.
#
# Graded (`partial(confidence)`): parse succeeds with warnings
# (deprecated syntax accepted by BuildKit v1 with deprecation
# notice), or LLB emission succeeds modulo a substrate-declared
# frontend normalisation; confidence carries the normalisation
# magnitude. The realisation decides whether to admit at the graded
# floor.
#
# Sibling composed bilaterals (15 landed): container_runnable,
# oci_well_formed, stagefreight_addressable, cascade_well_defined,
# audit_docblock, shatter_round_trip, third_order_coherent,
# three_axis_coherent, shift_preserves_content (TICK 2),
# image_shifted_from_oci (TICK 3), plus five others per Taut scout.
# The pattern is substrate-pull-confident; this shard adds the
# 16th instance at code altitude.
#
# Body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation composes the
# three sub-predicate verdicts at the substrate's three-state floor
# (pass / partial(confidence) / failure(reason)).
docker_buildable(d: dockerfile) -> verdict { \ }

# ============================================================
# §5 The out clauses
# ============================================================

out @facet/docker
out dockerfile
out build
out docker_buildable
